## Original Content
El Consejo de Ministros celebra su primera reunión tras el parón veraniego.

## Summary
The Spanish government has approved a single command in Ceuta to manage the return and repatriation of immigrants following a massive assault. This decision was made during the first Council of Ministers meeting after the summer break.

## Key Points
- The government established a single command structure in Ceuta.
- The command is focused on the return and repatriation of immigrants.
- The action is a response to a recent massive assault on Ceuta.
- The Council of Ministers made this approval in their first meeting after summer.


